# Publish safety

This repo is published as a clean public mirror. Armed git hooks enforce this;
do not work around them blindly.

## Never commit

- Secrets, tokens, API keys, credentials. Use `.env.local` (gitignored).
- Personal/machine paths or identifiers: local home paths, `op://` references,
  personal email handles. The `pre-commit` hook blocks these via patterns in
  the gitignored `.publish-guard.local`.
- Sensitive paths: `.env`, `.env.*`, `*op-refs.local.sh`,
  `*settings.local.json`, `.publish-guard.local`.

## If a hook blocks you

Fix the offending content — do not reflexively use `--no-verify`. Only override
(`git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify`) after reading the flagged
lines and confirming they are genuinely safe to publish. Treat an override as a
deliberate, logged decision.

## Pushing

- Only `main` may go to the public remote; the `pre-push` hook enforces this.
- Do not push to any public remote from an agent session unless explicitly
  asked by the user.
- Run `npm run verify` green before any push.

Full workflow and pre-publish checklist: `docs/PUBLISH-WORKFLOW.md`.
